turnkey-ruby (1:18.0-0) turnkey; urgency=low

  * Initial Ruby vertical for TurnKey Linux common.

  * rbenv + ruby-build installed to /usr/local/rbenv with jemalloc support.

  * System-wide rbenv availability via /etc/profile.d/rbenv.sh
    (works for all users, not just root).

  * Build-time conf/ruby script: sources by appliance conf.d/main with
    RUBY_VERSION variable to compile the required version.

  * Runtime tkl-upgrade-ruby helper script:
    - Interactive and non-interactive modes.
    - Auto-detects .ruby-version from known app paths
      (Mastodon, Rails, Redmine).
    - Updates ruby-build definitions before install.
    - Compiles with jemalloc and parallel make.
    - Cleanup command to remove old versions.

  * Extracted and generalized from conf/rails (which hardcoded
    RBY_VER=2.7.6 with no upgrade path).

  * Appliances using this vertical: conf/rails (refactored),
    Mastodon (new), Redmine (future).

